  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Boil the kettle. Add boiling water to a large saucepan with a pinch of salt.<br>• Add spaghetti to the boiling water and cook, over a high heat, until <br>‘al dente’, 9 minutes.<br>• Reserve pasta water(see ingredients). Drain spaghetti, then return to <br>saucepan. <br>TIP: ‘Al dente’ pasta is cooked through but still slightly firm in the centre.</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/68395864d9848b9dac05959a/step-d57ad100.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Meanwhile, thinly slice leek. Slice lemon into wedges.<br>• Heat a large frying pan over medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil.<br>• Cook leek, stirring, until softened, 4-5 minutes.<br>• Add garlic paste and garlic &amp; herb seasoning and cook until fragrant, <br>1 minute. Stir in light cooking cream, half of the Parmesan cheese, <br>the reserved pasta water and salt. Simmer until slightly thickened, <br>2-3 minutes. </p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/68395864d9848b9dac05959a/step-2eddea10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Stir in baby spinach leaves and cooked spaghetti to coat, until wilted, 1 <br>minute.<br>• Remove from heat, then add a good squeeze of lemon juice and a generous <br>pinch of pepper. <br>TIP: Seasoning is key in this dish, so taste and season with more salt and pepper <br>if needed. </p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/68395864d9848b9dac05959a/step-a1177e20.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Divide leek and spinach spaghetti alfredo between bowls.<br>• Top with remaining Parmesan cheese and a pinch of chilli flakes (if using). <br>Serve with remaining lemon wedges. Enjoy! </p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/68395864d9848b9dac05959a/step-84a04e30.jpg"
    }
  ]
